are assigned to component-named teams\nand should be verified by the strategy author.\n\n## Step 2: Component Graph\n\n| Component (canonical) | Classification | Rationale | Epics |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Feature Store | Active, NEW (no architecture-context file) | No productized repository, no build pipeline, no operator integration per problem statement → full onboarding chain (Rule 20) | E002 (repo), E003 (license), E004 (konflux), branch E007 (deployment) |\n| Platform Operator | Active, existing platform component | Already manages other components (\"like any other managed component\") — enablement integration only, no onboarding chain | branch E008 |\n| Dashboard | Active, existing (architecture context: `architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`, Konflux onboarded) | User-facing enablement of a component requires a Dashboard integration per architecture context | branch E009 |\n| Notebooks | Active, existing platform component — **not listed in Affected Components but required by HLR-2** (Feast SDK preinstalled in a supported workbench image) | Workbench images are the Notebooks component's surface; HLR coverage requires an epic | E005 |\n| Documentation | Active (content authoring) | HLR-4 requires new doc topics (enablement, getting-started, supported limits) — substantive authoring, not incidental touch-ups | E006 |\n\n**Component name mappings**: all assigned components use canonical names from\n`.context/rhai-components.txt` — no non-obvious mappings needed. The one\naddition beyond the strategy's list is **Notebooks** (see above), logged here as\na mapping note.\n\n**Architecture-context note**: only `dashboard.md` was provisioned in\n`.context/architecture-context/`. Feature Store has no file (expected — it is\nthe new component). Platform Operator, Notebooks, and Documentation also lack\nfiles; per the strategy's own description they are existing platform\ncomponents, so no onboarding chains were generated for them (see Health\nWarnings).\n\n## Step 3: Investigation Epics\n\nUnknowns scan (open questions table, risks, assumptions, pending reviews,\nconditional ADRs): exactly one genuine unknown — the deployment topology\n(Open Question 1).\n\n**Decision**: the answer changes which downstream epics exist and what they do\n(deployment mechanism, Platform Operator enablement mechanics, Dashboard\nreading surface all differ). → **Investigation epic E001**, gating all\ntopology-dependent Implementations. Bounded outcomes (2) → conditional\ndecomposition branches A (operator-based) and B (standalone server per\nproject).\n\nNot investigations: workbench-image SDK choice (HLR-2 is satisfiable either\nway — the Feast SDK is identical regardless of topology), license posture\n(scan-and-escalate, failure = remediation, not re-planning), docs topics\n(fixed by HLR-4 regardless of topology).\n\n## Epic List (main plan)\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E001 | Decide Feast deployment topology for productization | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E002 | Create midstream Feast repository under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E003 | License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E004 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the Feast repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E005 | Preinstall Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E006 | Feature Store product documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n\n### Branch epics (conditional, gated by E001 — not standalone Jira issues)\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E007 | Productize operator-based Feast deployment | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E008 | Enable Feature Store via Platform Operator (operator topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009 | Dashboard Feature Store presence and endpoint links (operator topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E007 | Productize standalone per-project Feast server | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E008 | Enable Feature Store via Platform Operator (per-project server topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E009 | Dashboard Feature Store presence and endpoint links (per-project server topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\nBranch nodes are conditional: exactly one of {A, B} executes, selected by the\nE001 outcome.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation: deployment topology\"]\n    E002[\"E002 repo-onboarding (midstream Feast repo)\"]\n    E003[\"E003 license-validation\"]\n    E004[\"E004 konflux-onboarding\"]\n    E005[\"E05 Feast SDK workbench image\"]\n    E006[\"E06 docs-authoring\"]\n    A_E007[\"BRANCH-A-E007 operator-based deployment\"]\n    A_E008[\"BRANCH-A-E008 Platform Operator enablement (A)\"]\n    A_E009[\"BRANCH-A-E009 Dashboard integration (A)\"]\n    B_E007[\"BRANCH-B-E007 standalone per-project server\"]\n    B_E008[\"BRANCH-B-E008 Platform Operator enablement (B)\"]\n    B_E009[\"BRANCH-B-E009 Dashboard integration (B)\"]\n\n    E002 --> E004\n    E002 --> A_E007\n    E002 --> B_E007\n    E003 --> E005\n    E003 --> A_E007\n    E003 --> B_E007\n    E001 --> A_E007\n    E001 --> B_E007\n    E001 --> A_E008\n    E001 --> B_E008\n    E001 --> A_E009\n    E001 --> B_E009\n    A_E007 --> A_E008\n    A_E007 --> A_E009\n    B_E007 --> B_E008\n    B_E007 --> B_E009\n    E001 --> E006\n    E002 --> E006\n    E003 --> E006\n    E004 --> E006\n    E005 --> E006\n```\n\nDeliberately absent edges (Rule 10)