t SDK is identical under both topologies; no gating |\n| (none) branch E008 ∥ branch E009 | Rule 14 | different repos, no shared artifacts |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n|---|---|---|\n| HLR-1 — admin enablement via Platform Operator with productized images | P0 | E001 (gating decision), E002, E003, E004 (productized-image chain), BRANCH-{A,B}-E007 (deployment), BRANCH-{A,B}-E008 (Platform Operator enablement) |\n| HLR-2 — Feast SDK preinstalled in a supported workbench image | P1 | E003 (license gate), E005 |\n| HLR-3 — Dashboard presence and per-project endpoint links | P1 | E001 (gating decision), BRANCH-{A,B}-E009 |\n| HLR-4 — product documentation (enablement, getting-started, limits) | P2 | E006 |\n\nAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Priority Inheritance\n\n- E001, E002, E003, E004 inherit P0: they (transitively) enable all HLR-1 work;\n  E003 blocks all P0 implementation.\n- Branch E007/E008 epics are P0 (HLR-1); branch E009 epics are P1 (HLR-3).\n- E006 is `docs-authoring`: exempt from inheritance; strategy frontmatter\n  `priority: Major` → P1.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing: Feast\nis upstream OSS being productized in-repo, and the only open question (topology)\nis an internal decision modeled as a conditional branch, not an external gate.\nPartial-value ordering emerges naturally: the onboarding chain (E002/E003/E004)\nand the workbench SDK image (E005) run topology-independent and are not blocked\nby the investigation.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies\n   table, no formal Acceptance Criteria, no NFRs. Acceptance criteria below are\n   derived from HLRs; team assignments are inferred (Dashboard from\n   architecture context; others are component-named placeholders) and should be\n   verified.\n2. **Architecture context incomplete**: only `dashboard.md` provisioned.\n   Platform O