-based OR standalone server per project) with\n  rationale, and reviewed by stakeholders.\n- The conditional implementation branch matching the decision is confirmed as\n  the plan of record; the non-selected branch is discarded.\n- Given the decision is made, when downstream teams start deployment,\n  enablement, and Dashboard work, then they have an unambiguous topology and\n  its per-project endpoint/CR surface — measured by the decision record being\n  referenced in those work items.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): gates the admin-enablement implementation path; the topology\n  decision determines how the Feature Store is deployed and enabled through\n  the Platform Operator.\n- HLR-3 (P1): determines the endpoint/CR surface the Dashboard will surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34057,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91b23b54818dce6f","agent_id":"a074d0cc1b5a9e09c","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"d80287f2-5528-4820-b265-53edc0acd522","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:33:27.183Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9006"}
