d team comes from the\n40\tarchitecture context file; other teams are assigned to component-named teams\n41\tand should be verified by the strategy author.\n42\t\n43\t## Step 2: Component Graph\n44\t\n45\t| Component (canonical) | Classification | Rationale | Epics |\n46\t|---|---|---|---|\n47\t| Feature Store | Active, NEW (no architecture-context file) | No productized repository, no build pipeline, no operator integration per problem statement → full onboarding chain (Rule 20) | E002 (repo), E003 (license), E004 (konflux), branch E007 (deployment) |\n48\t| Platform Operator | Active, existing platform component | Already manages other components (\"like any other managed component\") — enablement integration only, no onboarding chain | branch E008 |\n49\t| Dashboard | Active, existing (architecture context: `architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`, Konflux onboarded) | User-facing enablement of a component requires a Dashboard integration per architecture context | branch E009 |\n50\t| Notebooks | Active, existing platform component — **not listed in Affected Components but required by HLR-2** (Feast SDK preinstalled in a supported workbench image) | Workbench images are the Notebooks component's surface; HLR coverage requires an epic | E005 |\n51\t| Documentation | Active (content authoring) | HLR-4 requires new doc topics (enablement, getting-started, supported limits) — substantive authoring, not incidental touch-ups | E006 |\n52\t\n53\t**Component name mappings**: all assigned components use canonical names from\n54\t`.context/rhai-components.txt` — no non-obvious mappings needed. The one\n55\taddition beyond the strategy's list is **Notebooks** (see above), logged here as\n56\ta mapping note.\n57\t\n58\t**Architecture-context note**: only `dashboard.md` was provisioned in\n59\t`.context/architecture-context/`. Feature Store has no file (expected — it is\n60\tthe new component). Platform Operator, Notebooks, and Documentation also lack\n61\tfiles; per the strategy's own description they are existing platform\n62\tcomponents, so no onboarding chains were generated for them (see Health\n63\tWarnings).\n64\t\n65\t## Step 3: Investigation Epics\n66\t\n67\tUnknowns scan (open questions table, risks, assumptions, pending reviews,\n68\tconditional ADRs): exactly one genuine unknown — the deployment topology\n69\t(Open Question 1).\n70\t\n71\t**Decision**: the answer changes which downstream epics exist and what they do\n72\t(deployment mechanism, Platform Operator enablement mechanics, Dashboard\n73\treading surface all differ). → **Investigation epic E001**, gating all\n74\ttopology-dependent Implementations. Bounded outcomes (2) → conditional\n75\tdecomposition branches A (operator-based) and B (standalone server per\n76\tproject).\n77\t\n78\tNot investigations: workbench-image SDK choice (HLR-2 is satisfiable either\n79\tway — the Feast SDK is identical regardless of topology), license posture\n80\t(scan-and-escalate, failure = remediation, not re-planning), docs topics\n81\t(fixed by HLR-4 regardless of topology).\n82\t\n83\t## Epic List (main plan)\n84\t\n85\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n86\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n87\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E001 | Decide Feast deployment topology for productization | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n88\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E002 | Create midstream Feast repository under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n89\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E003 | License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n90\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E004 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the Feast repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n91\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E005 | Preinstall Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n92\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E006 | Feature Store product documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Doc