gests published by the build\n51\t  pipeline (pinned digests filled in as a configuration reference — an\n52\t  acceptance gate, not a build dependency).\n53\t- Provide disable/cleanup behavior consistent with other managed components.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a cluster with the Platform Operator installed, when an administrator\n58\t  enables the Feature Store, then the Feast operator is installed and the\n59\t  Feature Store becomes usable — measured by the same enablement flow used for\n60\t  other managed components.\n61\t- Disabling the Feature Store reconciles its resources away cleanly (rollback\n62\t  path for the enablement toggle).\n63\t- Enablement references pinned productized image digests that are available.\n64\t- The enablement behavior is verified on OpenShift against the productized\n65\t  operator-based deployment.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): administrators can enable a supported Feature Store through the\n70\t  Platform Operator like any other managed component.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10a0d1c266c9606","agent_id":"addcab36216e63e99","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"a6b6ef8f-48e5-46f6-b90f-f3ccdc1ed08c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:41:02.768Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce2c8462a4a8ab1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
