{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b98b3d8d1e9a234a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E007\n3\ttitle: Productize standalone per-project Feast server\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E003\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the standalone per-project server topology is not selected,\n18\t    this epic is removed and the operator-based deployment epic in the other branch\n19\t    executes instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 0\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 2\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Productize standalone per-project Feast server\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConditional epic — executes only if the deployment-topology investigation\n41\tselects the standalone server per project. Productize the per-project Feast\n42\tserver as the supported deployment mechanism for the Feature Store: each\n43\tproject gets its own Feast server instance, built from the productized\n44\tmidstream repository and shipped as Konflux-built container images.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Productize the standalone Feast server for per-project deployment on\n49\t    OpenShift: packaging, manifests, and lifecycle for server instances\n50\t    provisioned per project, against the midstream Feast codebase.\n51\t- Consume the productized images built by the Konflux pipeline (pinned\n52\t    digests are a configuration reference wired at execution time — the\n53\t    deployment code is not blocked on the pipeline beyond the green-build\n54\t    gate below).\n55\t- Define the resource/API surface a per-project server instance exposes,\n56\t    which the Platform Operator enablement and the Dashboard integration\n57\t    build against.\n58\t- Document failure modes, upgrade path, and per-project isolation behavior\n59\t    for supportability.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A productized Feast server can be deployed per project on OpenShift and\n64\t  reaches a running, usable state.\n65\t- The build pipeline is green for all images shipped by this deployment (the\n66\t  Konflux pipeline builds the merged implementation code successfully).\n67\t- Productized image digests are published and pinnable by consumers.\n68\t- Failure modes, upgrade behavior, and per-project isolation are documented\n69\t  sufficiently for the supportability standard used by the topology decision.\n70\t- Given the standalone per-project server is productized, when enablement and\n71\t  Dashboard work consume its resource surface, then that surface is stable\n72\t  and documented.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): provides the deployable, supported Feature Store with\n77\t  productized images that administrators enable through the Platform Operator.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10a0d1c266c9606","agent_id":"addcab36216e63e99","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"6102ba69-769d-47ff-a86b-f4a1dd75cf9d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:41:05.405Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b98b3d8d1e9a234a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
