\t- Follow the Dashboard's existing component-integration pattern (per-component\n52\t  feature flags and defaults via the dashboard configuration CR, reading\n53\t  component CRs via the Kubernetes API).\n54\t- No feature-authoring UI: navigation and link-out only.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given the Feature Store is enabled for a project, when a user opens the\n59\t  Dashboard, then the Feature Store appears as an enabled component for that\n60\t  project — measured by the enabled-components view.\n61\t- Endpoint links resolve to that project's Feast server instance under the\n62\t  per-project server deployment.\n63\t- The integration is feature-flagged/configurable via the Dashboard\n64\t  configuration CR consistent with other component integrations.\n65\t- No feature-authoring UI is introduced (link-out only, per out-of-scope).\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-3 (P1): the Dashboard shows the Feature Store as an enabled component\n70\t  and links users to its endpoints per project.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10a0d1c266c9606","agent_id":"addcab36216e63e99","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"e3581356-8dd7-4480-8768-bb1a7f99b129","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:41:07.996Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0f77a08961d2f25","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
