{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93128a368d6c6ed6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9006\n3\tscore: 13\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n9\t  description: 'E004 (konflux-onboarding) scores human_process_gates: 0 with a hedged\n10\t    rationale (\"no explicit human approval step assumed\") while the analogous org-level\n11\t    action in the same onboarding chain, E002 repo creation, scores -1 for maintainer/org\n12\t    approval; Konflux application/namespace provisioning is comparably likely to require\n13\t    an admin request, so the 0 is arguable — re-score or justify the asymmetry.'\n14\terror: null\n15\t---\n16\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9006\n17\t\n18\t## Review Summary\n19\t\n20\tScore: 13/14 — pass\n21\tRecommendation: accept\n22\t\n23\t## Criterion Details\n24\t\n25\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n26\t\n27\tAll four HLRs map to epics, and the traceability matrix in the decomposition\n28\tsummary is complete:\n29\t\n30\t- HLR-1 (P0): E001, E002, E003, E004, BRANCH-{A,B}-E007, BRANCH-{A,B}-E008.\n31\t- HLR-2 (P1): E003, E005 — correctly identified Notebooks as a required\n32\t  component beyond the strategy's Affected Components list (workbench images\n33\t  are the Notebooks surface), logged as a health warning.\n34\t- HLR-3 (P1): E001, BRANCH-{A,B}-E009.\n35\t- HLR-4 (P2): E006, covered (not deferred, though deferral would have been\n36\t  permissible).\n37\t\n38\tPriority inheritance is correct: E001–E004 are P0 enabling all HLR-1 work;\n39\tbranch E007/E008 are P0 (HLR-1), branch E009 is P1 (HLR-3); E006 is\n40\tdocs-authoring and correctly exempt (strategy priority Major → P1). No\n41\tinversions. No priority collapse: E003's mapping to both HLR-1 and HLR-2 is a\n42\tsingle license-validation work item, not a bundle of deferrable features; E001\n43\tis a single investigation. Triage is null (full decomposition), so multi-epic\n44\toutput is expected.\n45\t\n46\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n47\t\n48\tVerified every diagram edge against epic frontmatter `dependencies` and vice\n49\tversa — all 21 edges match exactly, arrows drawn dependency → dependent per\n50\tconvention. No circular dependencies. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic in\n51\tits dependencies; all six branch files set both `branch` (A/B, matching\n52\tfilename) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001`. Both bounded outcomes of the\n53\ttopology question have branch epics.\n54\t\n55\tImplementation-type parallelism correctly enforced:\n56\t\n57\t- No `konflux-onboarding → general implementation` edge: E004 has edges only\n58\t  from E002; branch E007/E008/E009 and E005 have no edge to/from E004. The\n59\t  coupling is correctly carried as the Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC on the\n60\t  branch E007 epics (and E005), and image digests are explicitly treated as\n61\t  configuration references (AC gates), not DAG edges.\n62\t- No `license-validation → repo-onboarding` or `license-validation →\n63\t  konflux-onboarding` edges (E003 deps empty; E004 deps only E002).\n64\t- E002 → E004 is the mandated Rule 5 serial onboarding edge.\n65\t\n66\tRule 13 edges (branch E007 → branch E008/E009) are justified as build-against\n67\tCRD/API-surface dependencies, distinct from config references. The absent\n68\tE008–E009 edge is justified under Rule 14 (different repos, no shared\n69\tbuild-against artifacts; the Dashboard reads CRs defined by E007, which it\n70\tdepends on). Critical path length 3 (E002→E004→E006) is consistent with — in\n71\tfact slightly more parallel than — the M-with-new-component heuristic; shorter\n72\tis not a defect.\n73\t\n74\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n75\t\n76\tEvery epic is a single component/team tuple: Feature Store (E001–E004, branch\n77\tE007s), Platform Operator (branch E008s), Dashboard (branch E009s), Notebooks\n78\t(E005), Documentation (E006). No cross-team bundling. The apparent duplication\n79\tbetween branch A and branch B epics is the conditional-branch design\n80\t(mutually exclusive alternatives), not sibling scope duplication. Work-product\n81\ttypes are properly separated: docs authoring (E006) is its own epic, and the\n82\tonboarding chain (repo/license/konflux) is split per type. No epic exceeds\n83\tsprint scale.\n84\t\n85\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n86\t\n87\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome selects which conditional branch\n88\texists (operator-based vs standalone per-project), changing downstream epic\n89\texistence and scope. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts.\n90\tEvery epic with `gated_by` has both `action` and `fallback_approach` populated\n91\t(branch epics: remove + other-branch replacement; E006: rewrite + re-scope to\n92\tselected topology — a genuine scope change, not a bare scheduling dependency).\n93\tEvery epic listing the Investigation E001 in `dependencies` also sets\n94\t`gated_by` to it, and every `gated_by` target is in that epic's direct\n95\t`dependencies` list.\n96\t\n97\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n98\t\n99\tSignal-type discipline is correct: E001 (Investigation) carries\n100\t`investigation_signals` only; all Implementation epics carry `ai_signals`\n101\tonly. All 13 rationale files are present, and every frontmatter signal value\n102\tmatches its rationale-file value. E001's `source_accessibility: 1` is\n103\tjustified — the evidence base (upstream Feast source/docs) is public, and the\n104\thuman sign-off is separately captured by `human_judgment_required: -1`.\n105\t`open_questions: 1` on E002–E005 is justified: the topology question\n106\texplicitly does not change those epics' approach (SDK identical, repo/scan/\n107\tpipeline topology-agnostic), and branch epics correctly score 0 with the gate\n108\tresolved before start.\n109\t\n110\tOne arguable value: E004 (`konflux-onboarding`) scores `human_process_gates:\n111\t0` with a rationale that explicitly hedges (\"no explicit human approval step\n112\tassumed\"), while the analogous org-level action in the same onboarding chain —\n113\tE002's repo creation under opendatahub-io — scores -1 for maintainer/org\n114\tapproval. Konflux application/namespace provisioning is comparably likely to\n115\tinvolve an admin request, so the 0 is arguable and the rationale is thin.\n116\t\n117\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n118\t\n119\tEvery epic has testable ACs, most in Given/When/Then form with stated\n120\tmeasurement. Rule-mandated ACs are present everywhere applicable: E006 has\n121\tthe technical-review-by-implementing-teams AC (Rule 24); both branch E007\n122\tepics and E005 carry build-pipeline-green ACs (Rule 25), and E004's own ACs\n123\tcover green builds with published digests; branch E008 epics include\n124\tdisable/cleanup (rollback-path) ACs; branch E009 epics include feature-flag\n125\tconfigurability. No epic body references sibling epics by bare draft ID —\n126\tcross-references use descriptive names (\"the topology investigation\", \"the\n127\tconsuming implementation\"), with full epic IDs confined to structured\n128\tfrontmatter.\n129\t\n130\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n131\t\n132\tThe combined epic set covers the full strategy scope: productization chain\n133\t(E002/E003/E004), deployment (branch E007s), Platform Operator enablement\n134\t(HLR-1, branch E008s), workbench SDK reachability (HLR-2, E005), Dashboard\n135\tpresence and per-project endpoint links (HLR-3, branch E009s), and\n136\tdocumentation (HLR-4, E006). The single open question is modeled as\n137\tInvestigation E001 with conditional branches covering both stated bounded\n138\toutcomes. Out-of-scope statements are carried forward correctly: link-out-only\n139\tDashboard (E009 ACs) and bring-your-own offline store as a documented supported\n140\tlimit (E006 scope/ACs) rather than dropped or silently implemented. The\n141\tstrategy's missing sections (teams, dependencies, formal ACs, NFRs) are\n142\texplicitly logged as health warnings with inferred team assignments flagged\n143\tfor verification rather than silently assumed.\n144\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a89f9ff1644c616","agent_id":"af55acb7308737cf7","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"352b7796-724d-4797-9c84-17b9a6ca7af7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:46:16.938Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93128a368d6c6ed6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
