y's own description they are existing platform\n62\tcomponents, so no onboarding chains were generated for them (see Health\n63\tWarnings).\n64\t\n65\t## Step 3: Investigation Epics\n66\t\n67\tUnknowns scan (open questions table, risks, assumptions, pending reviews,\n68\tconditional ADRs): exactly one genuine unknown — the deployment topology\n69\t(Open Question 1).\n70\t\n71\t**Decision**: the answer changes which downstream epics exist and what they do\n72\t(deployment mechanism, Platform Operator enablement mechanics, Dashboard\n73\treading surface all differ). → **Investigation epic E001**, gating all\n74\ttopology-dependent Implementations. Bounded outcomes (2) → conditional\n75\tdecomposition branches A (operator-based) and B (standalone server per\n76\tproject).\n77\t\n78\tNot investigations: workbench-image SDK choice (HLR-2 is satisfiable either\n79\tway — the Feast SDK is identical regardless of topology), license posture\n80\t(scan-and-escalate, failure = remediation, not re-planning), docs topics\n81\t(fixed by HLR-4 regardless of topology).\n82\t\n83\t## Epic List (main plan)\n84\t\n85\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n86\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n87\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E001 | Decide Feast deployment topology for productization | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n88\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E002 | Create midstream Feast repository under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n89\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E003 | License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n90\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E004 | Konflux build pipeline onboarding for the Feast repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n91\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E005 | Preinstall Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n92\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E006 | Feature Store product documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n93\t\n94\t### Branch epics (conditional, gated by E001 — not standalone Jira issues)\n95\t\n96\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n97\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n98\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E007 | Productize operator-based Feast deployment | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n99\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E008 | Enable Feature Store via Platform Operator (operator topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n100\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009 | Dashboard Feature Store presence and endpoint links (operator topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n101\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E007 | Productize standalone per-project Feast server | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n102\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E008 | Enable Feature Store via Platform Operator (per-project server topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n103\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E009 | Dashboard Feature Store presence and endpoint links (per-project server topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n104\t\n105\t## Dependency DAG\n106\t\n107\tBranch nodes are conditional: exactly one of {A, B} executes, selected by the\n108\tE001 outcome.\n109\t\n110\t```mermaid\n111\tgraph TD\n112\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: deployment topology\"]\n113\t    E002[\"E002 repo-onboarding (midstream Feast repo)\"]\n114\t    E003[\"E003 license-validation\"]\n115\t    E004[\"E004 konflux-onboarding\"]\n116\t    E005[\"E05 Feast SDK workbench image\"]\n117\t    E006[\"E06 docs-authoring\"]\n118\t    A_E007[\"BRANCH-A-E007 operator-based deployment\"]\n119\t    A_E008[\"BRANCH-A-E008 Platform Operator enablement (A)\"]\n120\t    A_E009[\"BRANCH-A-E009 Dashboard integration (A)\"]\n121\t    B_E007[\"BRANCH-B-E007 standalone per-project server\"]\n122\t    B_E008[\"BRANCH-B-E008 Platform Operator enablement (B)\"]\n123\t    B_E009[\"BRANCH-B-E009 Dashboard integration (B)\"]\n124\t\n125\t    E002 --> E004\n126\t    E002 --> A_E007\n127\t    E002 --> B_E007\n128\t    E003 --> E005\n129\t    E003 --> A_E007\n130\t    E003 --> B_E007\n131\t    E001 --> A_E007\n132\t    E001 --> B_E007\n133\t    E001 --> A_E008\n134\t    E001 --> B_E008\n135\t    E001 --> A_E009\n136\t    E001 --> B_E009\n137\t    A_E007 --> A_E008\n138\t    A_E007 --> A_E009\n139\t    B_E007 --> B_E008\n140\t    B_E007 --> B_E009\n141\t    E001 --> E006\n142\t    E002 --> E006\n143\t    E003 --> E006\n144\t    E004 --> E006\n145\t    E005 --> E006\n146\t```\n147\t\n148\tDeliberately absent edges (Rule 10): no `E004 → branch E007` edge —\n149\tkonflux-onboarding runs parallel to the general implementation; the coupling is\n150\tenforced by the \"build pipeline green\" AC on the deployment epics. No edge\n151\tbetween branch E008 (Platform Operator) and branch E009 (Dashboard) — different\n152\trepos, no shared build-against artifacts (Rule 14).\n153\t\n154\t## DAG Justification\n155\t\n156\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n157\t|---|---|---|\n158\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding always serial; pipeline needs the repo |\n159\t| E002 → BRANCH-{A,B}-E007 | Rule 6 | deployment implementation needs the onboarded repo; does not block other repos |\n160\t| E003 → BRANCH-{A,B}-E007 | Rule 9 | license failure changes the dependency set and the productization approach |\n161\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 9 | the workbench image bakes in the Feast SDK and its transitive deps; license failure changes what can ship |\n162\t| E001 → BRANCH-{A,B}-E007/E008/E009 | Rule 3 | topology decision gates existence and scope of deployment, enablement, and Dashboard work; true gates recorded via `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` |\n163\t| BRANCH-X-E007 → BRANCH-X-E008 | Rule 13 | Platform Operator enablement builds against the Feast deployment's CRDs/manifests (build-against artifact, not a config reference) |\n164\t| BRANCH-X-E007 → BRANCH-X-E009 | Rule 13 | Dashboard reads the CRs and endpoints the deployment exposes |\n165\t| E002, E003, E004, E005, E001 → E006 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics; E001 (Investigation) also included so docs reflect the selected topology — branch epics cannot appear in main-plan dependencies, and the \"technically reviewed against implementation\" AC (Rule 24) covers the executed branch |\n166\t| (none) E004 ∥ E002-parallel work, E003 ∥ E004, E004 ∥ branch E007 | Rules 7, 8, 10 | license-validation parallel to repo-onboarding and konflux-onboarding; konflux-onboarding parallel to general implementation — image digests consumed downstream are AC gates, not DAG edges |\n167\t| (none) E005 ∥ E001 | — | the Feast SDK is identical under both topologies; no gating |\n168\t| (none) branch E008 ∥ branch E009 | Rule 14 | different repos, no shared artifacts |\n169\t\n170\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n171\t\n172\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n173\t|---|---|---|\n174\t| HLR-1 — admin enablement via Platform Operator with productized images | P0 | E001 (gating decision), E002, E003, E004 (productized-image chain), BRANCH-{A,B}-E007 (deployment), BRANCH-{A,B}-E008 (Platform Operator enablement) |\n175\t| HLR-2 — Feast SDK preinstalled in a supported workbench image | P1 | E003 (license gate), E005 |\n176\t| HLR-3 — Dashboard presence and per-project endpoint links | P1 | E001 (gating decision), BRANCH-{A,B}-E009 |\n177\t| HLR-4 — product documentation (enablement, getting-started, limits) | P2 | E006 |\n178\t\n179\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n180\t\n181\t## Priority Inheritance\n182\t\n183\t- E001, E002, E003, E004 inherit P0: they (transitively) enable all HLR-1 work;\n184\t  E003 blocks all P0 implementation.\n185\t- Branch E007/E008 epics are P0 (HLR-1); branch E009 epics are P1 (HLR-3).\n186\t- E006 is `docs-authoring`: exempt from inheritance; strategy frontmatter\n187\t  `priority: Major` → P1.\n188\t\n189\t## Tiered Delivery\n190\t\n191\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing: Feast\n192\tis upstream OSS being productized in-repo, and the only open question (topology)\n193\tis an internal decision modeled as a conditional branch, not an external gate.\n194\tPartial-value ordering emerges naturally: the onboarding chain (E002/E003/E004)\n195\tand the workbench SDK image (E005) run topology-independent and are not blocked\n196\tby the investigation.\n197\t\n198\t## Health Warnings\n199\t\n200\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies\n201\t   table, no formal Acceptance Criteria, no NFRs. Acceptance criteria below are\n202\t   derived from HLRs; team assignments are inferred (Dashboard from\n203\t   architecture context; others are component-named placeholders) and should be\n204\t   verified.\n205\t2. **Architecture context incomplete**: only `dashboard.md` provisioned.\n206\t   Platform Operator, Notebooks, and Documentation have no files but are\n207\t   existing platform components per the strategy text — no onboarding chains\n208\t   generated for them. If any is actually absent from the platform inventory,\n209\t   Rule 20/22 chains would be needed.\n210\t3. **Component added beyond Affected Components list**: Notebooks (E005),\n211\t   required for HLR-2 coverage (workbench images).\n212\t4. **Scope trap (informational)**: HLR-3's \"links users to its endpoints per\n213\t   project\" must respect the out-of-scope feature-authoring UI — Dashboard work\n214\t   is link-out only. Out-of-scope \"managed offline-store infrastructure\" means\n215\t   docs must state bring-your-own storage as a supported limit, not an NFR to\n216\t   satisfy.\n217\t5. No priority inversions detected.\n218\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeae706774aaacc5","agent_id":"a1f0a18dd6ef1c5d7","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"8f0427ba-7bfb-425e-8119-cc5bb1d14012","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:48:29.144Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92355126dbd12096","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","