{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d22e7e604120acf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n3\ttitle: Decide Feast deployment topology for productization\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide Feast deployment topology for productization\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's open question: which Feast deployment topology to\n30\tproductize first — the operator-based deployment or the standalone server per\n31\tproject. Upstream Feast supports both; their supportability profiles differ\n32\t(upgrade path, per-project isolation, resource footprint, failure modes, and\n33\tfit with the Platform Operator's managed-component enablement model). This\n34\tinvestigation produces the decision and the supportability assessment behind\n35\tit, and selects which conditional implementation branch executes.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Assess both candidate topologies against defined supportability criteria:\n40\t  upgrade/version management, per-project isolation and multi-tenancy,\n41\t  resource footprint, failure modes and operational burden, alignment with how\n42\t  the Platform Operator enables other managed components, and Dashboard\n43\t  integration surface (what CRs/endpoints each topology exposes per project).\n44\t- Use upstream Feast documentation, repository source, and deployment\n45\t  references as evidence; validate operator-rendered resources from source\n46\t  where possible.\n47\t- Record the decision with rationale and obtain stakeholder/product sign-off\n48\t  on the selected topology.\n49\t- Confirm the downstream impact: which deployment, Platform Operator\n50\t  enablement, and Dashboard integration work proceeds under the selected\n51\t  outcome.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Both topologies are assessed against the enumerated supportability criteria,\n56\t  with evidence drawn from upstream source and documentation.\n57\t- A decision is recorded (operator-based OR standalone server per project) with\n58\t  rationale, and reviewed by stakeholders.\n59\t- The conditional implementation branch matching the decision is confirmed as\n60\t  the plan of record; the non-selected branch is discarded.\n61\t- Given the decision is made, when downstream teams start deployment,\n62\t  enablement, and Dashboard work, then they have an unambiguous topology and\n63\t  its per-project endpoint/CR surface — measured by the decision record being\n64\t  referenced in those work items.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-1 (P0): gates the admin-enablement implementation path; the topology\n69\t  decision determines how the Feature Store is deployed and enabled through\n70\t  the Platform Operator.\n71\t- HLR-3 (P1): determines the endpoint/CR surface the Dashboard will surface.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeae706774aaacc5","agent_id":"a1f0a18dd6ef1c5d7","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"0255158c-d0f0-4343-af45-b1c5455a2a26","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:48:34.339Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d22e7e604120acf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
