ry's upstream sync and midstream patch policy.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A midstream Feast repository exists under opendatahub-io, derived from\n54\t  upstream Feast, with the midstream branching/rebase workflow in place.\n55\t- The repository builds from source (the imported code compiles/packages as\n56\t  upstream documents).\n57\t- The repository's sync/patch policy is documented in the repository.\n58\t- Given the repository exists, when build-pipeline onboarding and deployment\n59\t  implementation begin, then they have a canonical productized source\n60\t  repository to build from.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P0): prerequisite for productized Feature Store images and any\n65\t  supported deployment; enables all downstream Feature Store implementation.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeae706774aaacc5","agent_id":"a1f0a18dd6ef1c5d7","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"d6e67447-b52f-4e03-86ec-fd33c8995fdd","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:48:35.520Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfc8ce5f332d2ed7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
