te license scan of Feast and its transitive dependency tree exists,\n53\t  with a triage report covering every flagged license.\n54\t- No unresolved license conflict remains that blocks shipping the Feast SDK in\n55\t  workbench images or the Feature Store server/operator images — any\n56\t  conflicts are either cleared or have a documented remediation plan accepted\n57\t  by stakeholders.\n58\t- Given the scan is clear, when the workbench SDK image and the deployment\n59\t  implementation proceed, then their dependency sets are license-cleared for\n60\t  productization.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P0): productized Feature Store images require license-cleared\n65\t  dependencies.\n66\t- HLR-2 (P1): the Feast SDK cannot ship in a supported workbench image unless\n67\t  its dependency tree is license-cleared.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeae706774aaacc5","agent_id":"a1f0a18dd6ef1c5d7","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"1e18b950-8bc0-45ca-82bd-93f085315a39","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:48:36.680Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac6021ff159fe6f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
