{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdc095113717b61f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E005\n3\ttitle: Preinstall Feast SDK in a supported workbench image\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: RHOAI Notebooks\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E003\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Preinstall Feast SDK in a supported workbench image\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tMake the feature store reachable from workbenches (HLR-2) by preinstalling\n35\tthe Feast Python SDK in at least one supported RHOAI workbench image, so data\n36\tscientists can connect to the Feature Store without manual installation. The\n37\tFeast SDK is identical regardless of which deployment topology is productized,\n38\tso this work is not gated by the topology decision — only by license clearance\n39\tof the SDK's dependency tree.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Select at least one supported workbench image (e.g. the standard data\n44\t  science image) to carry the Feast SDK preinstalled.\n45\t- Add the Feast SDK package and its dependencies to the image build.\n46\t- Verify the SDK imports and can be configured against a Feast deployment\n47\t  endpoint from within a workbench.\n48\t- Update the image's package manifest/version metadata per image conventions.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- At least one supported workbench image ships with the Feast SDK\n53\t  preinstalled, listed in the image's package manifest.\n54\t- Given a workbench spawned from that image, when a data scientist runs\n55\t  `import feast` and points the SDK at a Feature Store endpoint, then the SDK\n56\t  loads and connects — measured by a smoke test executed in a spawned\n57\t  workbench.\n58\t- The SDK's transitive dependencies are license-cleared for productization\n59\t  (blocked-by relationship on the license validation work).\n60\t- The workbench image build pipeline is green with the change merged.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P1): data scientists can reach the feature store from workbenches\n65\t  with the Feast SDK preinstalled in at least one supported workbench image.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeae706774aaacc5","agent_id":"a1f0a18dd6ef1c5d7","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"33775e8a-a92a-4977-a665-67d42b50ace0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:48:38.946Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdc095113717b61f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
