er deployment\n51\t  exposes.\n52\t- Wire enablement to the productized image digests published by the build\n53\t  pipeline (pinned digests filled in as a configuration reference — an\n54\t  acceptance gate, not a build dependency).\n55\t- Provide disable/cleanup behavior consistent with other managed components.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a cluster with the Platform Operator installed, when an administrator\n60\t  enables the Feature Store, then per-project Feast server instances can be\n61\t  provisioned and used — measured by the same enablement flow used for other\n62\t  managed components.\n63\t- Disabling the Feature Store reconciles its resources away cleanly (rollback\n64\t  path for the enablement toggle).\n65\t- Enablement references pinned productized image digests that are available.\n66\t- The enablement behavior is verified on OpenShift against the productized\n67\t  per-project server deployment.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P0): administrators can enable a supported Feature Store through the\n72\t  Platform Operator like any other managed component.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeae706774aaacc5","agent_id":"a1f0a18dd6ef1c5d7","session_id":"70be5069-4ad1-4d5f-b439-3a3690791b3e","uuid":"d03e4d2b-a7b1-40ff-9508-4e21c0ca94a9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:48:50.017Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a46ca2167a605caa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
